Statements:
[
    "LLM agents for education combine core components like memory, tool use, and planning to enhance performance for diverse tasks.",
    "Education, a field inherently focused on individualized learning and problem-solving, is one of the ideal scenarios for deploying LLM agents.",
    "Long-term memory enables the agent to retain an understanding of fundamental concepts and store personalized profiles to provide accurate responses.",
    "Short-term memory supports real-time adaptation, enabling context-aware interactions.",
    "Techniques such as summarization and retrieval help maintain relevant information.",
    "The memory module tracks the student's past interactions and progress.",
    "LLM agents integrate external tools like search engines, calculators, and databases to overcome LLM limitations, such as knowledge cutoff and calculation inefficiency.",
    "The tool-use module allows the agent to access specialized educational tools, such as knowledge tracing and recommendation models, as well as external resources, thereby expanding its functional capabilities.",
    "Planning capabilities allow agents to decompose goals, simulate state transitions, and optimize actions for complex problem-solving.",
    "LLM agents can automate tasks, making it possible to build self-sustaining adaptive learning systems without teacher involvement.",
    "These systems operate within an action-memory framework, continuously refining instruction based on student profiling, content selection, and difficulty adaptation.",
    "All traditional attacks like PGD and MI-FGSM use the sign function to scale their perturbations, which raises several theoretical concerns from the point of view of optimization.",
    "PGD is actually a specific reformulation of the projected gradient method using only the current gradient to determine its step-size.",
    "When a conventional adaptive matrix with accumulated gradients is utilized to scale the perturbation, PGD becomes AdaGrad.",
    "The proposed AdaMI attack optimizes the perturbation with a momentum-based adaptive matrix instead of the sign function and the conventional gradient-based matrix.",
    "AdaMI is proved to attain optimal convergence for convex problems, indicating that it addresses the non-convergence issue of MI-FGSM, thereby ensuring stability of the optimization process.",
    "The connection between MI-FGSM and AdaMI is completely similar to the correlation between PGD and AdaGrad.",
    "AdaMI can effectively keep the transferability of MI-FGSM by using only the EMA of past momentums.",
    "The momentum-based adaptive matrix can serve as a general and effective technique to boost adversarial transferability over state-of-the-art methods."
] 

