Statements:
[
    "The success of modern multimodal representation learning relies on internet-scale datasets.",
    "Due to the low quality of a large fraction of raw web data, data curation has become a critical step in the training pipeline.",
    "In vision-language data, a significant portion of the misalignment arises randomly.",
    "Images are paired with irrelevant or tangentially related captions due to the processes of automated web scraping and the uncontrolled nature of internet data.",
    "The theoretical analysis adopts a stochastic corruption model where a fraction η of pairs are correctly aligned, while the remaining 1−η fraction has mismatched modalities.",
    "This stochastic corruption model is more relevant in capturing the nature of real data compared to adversarial corruption models used in robust statistics.",
    "The error of unfiltered contrastive learning with n samples and η clean fraction depends as 1/η√n.",
    "This is established through an upper bound from prior work.",
    "A matching lower bound makes this rate tight.",
    "For teacher-based filtering, the dependency on η is dramatically improved.",
    "In the large η regime, the error bound is 1/√ηn.",
    "In the small η regime, the error bound is 1/√n (independent of η).",
    "The improvement from 1/η to 1/√η in the large η regime represents a significant gain.",
    "In the small η regime, performance becomes independent of η entirely.",
    "Teacher-based filtering can be particularly beneficial when data quality is low, achieving performance independent of the initial clean fraction.",
    "Teacher-based filtering leverages a pre-trained model to compute quality scores.",
    "The intuition is that filtering can identify corrupted samples and remove them, effectively increasing the clean fraction in the training data.",
    "The theoretical results include the training of the teacher model on the given dataset.",
    "They do not assume the existence of any strong pre-trained model.",
    "The theoretical predictions have been verified empirically.",
    "Synthetic experiments verify the 1/η dependence of unfiltered contrastive learning.",
    "They also confirm the improved dependence achieved by teacher-based filtering: 1/√η for large η and independent of η for small η.",
    "The qualitative observation of improved η dependence via filtering holds true even with real data.",
    "These results provide a formal basis for the empirical success of teacher-based data filtering.",
    "The provable benefit comes from transforming a harsh 1/η error dependency into a much milder 1/√η or even η-independent error rate.",
    "This makes learning feasible even when a substantial portion of the training data is corrupted."
] 

