Statements:
[
    "Existing approaches to learning dynamics typically either discretize time—leading to poor performance on irregularly sampled data—or ignore the underlying causality.",
    "Most state-of-the-art methods for causal discovery on time-series focus on learning the causal structure, but rarely capture the underlying continuous dynamics.",
    "Most methods learn a discretized version of the true dynamics while assuming regular sampling, and are not designed for irregularly-sampled data.",
    "Discrete-time approaches include constraint-based methods, score-based methods, and noise-based methods, all of which assume regularly sampled discrete trajectories and overlook the continuous-time structure of time series.",
    "Real-world physical systems are fundamentally governed by continuous-time dynamics with intrinsic causal mechanisms.",
    "In a mass-spring system, the position of each mass induces a force influencing its own velocity and the velocities of other masses connected to it with a spring.",
    "CADYT leverages the Gaussian Process-based framework developed by Ensinger et al. (2024) to learn a continuous-time model of the dynamics.",
    "The method leverages the Gaussian Process framework for exact inference in continuous time, enabling nonparametric modeling of system dynamics.",
    "CADYT leverages exact Gaussian Process inference for modeling the continuous-time dynamics which is more aligned with the underlying dynamical process.",
    "The method proposed by Ensinger et al. (2024) is leveraged due to the beneficial properties of exact inference even under irregular sampling.",
    "Dynamic-systems modeling approaches that adapt to irregularly-sampled data by learning a continuous-time model exist, but these methods ignore causality and do not guarantee the generalization capabilities of causal models.",
    "In contrast to state-of-the-art causal discovery methods that model the problem using discrete-time Dynamic Bayesian networks, CADYT's formulation is grounded in Difference-based causal models, which allow milder assumptions for modeling the continuous nature of the system.",
    "Difference-based causal models (DBCM) differ from well-known dynamic Bayesian networks in that they force all causation to go through derivatives.",
    "CADYT uses these Difference-based Causal Models as opposed to Dynamic Bayesian Networks.",
    "The approach aims to find the underlying directed graph G of process interactions entailed by the DSCM and learn the dynamics of each variable using only its causal parents.",
    "The method assumes causal sufficiency (no unobserved confounders) and that G is µ-Markovian with respect to the trajectory T.",
    "CADYT incorporates a novel score that leverages the Algorithmic Markov Condition (AMC) postulate.",
    "AMC allows identification of the causes of a target variable as the ones providing the simplest description, in terms of Kolmogorov complexity.",
    "The score upper bounds the otherwise uncomputable Kolmogorov complexity via the Minimum Description Length principle.",
    "CADYT is an end-to-end algorithm combining Gaussian Process dynamical system modeling methods for continuous-time inference with structure search, enabling exact evaluation of dynamics while recovering true causal mechanisms.",
    "The algorithm uses a general greedy structure search incorporating the proposed score into a common three-step search procedure: edge scoring, forward and backward search.",
    "CADYT outperforms state-of-the-art methods on both regularly and irregularly-sampled data, discovering causal networks closer to the true underlying dynamics.",
    "For random graphs of sizes D ∈ {5, 10, 15}, CADYT finds graphs closer to the ground truth, resulting in a lower Normalized Structural Hamming Distance (NSHD) for both regularly sampled data and irregularly sampled data.",
    "The learned continuous-time model adapts to arbitrary timelines, including irregularly sampled ones.",
    "This is a key advantage over discrete-time methods that struggle with non-uniform sampling.",
    "CADYT addresses two challenges previously tackled in isolation: irregular sampling and causal structure identification.",
    "By combining GP-based continuous-time modeling with principled causal discovery through the Algorithmic Markov Condition, CADYT provides a unified framework that respects both the continuous nature of real-world dynamics and the importance of discovering true causal relationships."
] 

