Statements:
[
    "AnySleep blends U-Net-inspired encoder-decoder architecture with channel-attention modules for high-frequency sleep staging.",
    "The design allows for handling any number and choice of EEG and EOG channels.",
    "Each input channel is processed by successive encoder blocks to yield channel-specific feature maps at increasing levels of abstraction.",
    "Channel-attention modules combine an arbitrary number of channel-specific feature maps into cross-channel representations based on learnable attention weights.",
    "AnySleep is a deep neural network that can dynamically combine any available EEG or EOG channels to score sleep at flexible temporal resolutions.",
    "AnySleep required no manual work to define channel modalities compared to U-Sleep.",
    "AnySleep matched or surpassed U-Sleep's performance across all tested channel configurations and datasets.",
    "AnySleep showed robust performance across diverse channel configurations, including cases with missing EOG or EEG channels.",
    "Performance improved as more channels were provided.",
    "Model performance remained stable when evaluated across two-channel permutations.",
    "AnySleep maintained strong performance even in single-channel configurations.",
    "U-Sleep's practical utility is limited by its deliberately fixed input modality and channel requirements.",
    "U-Sleep expects a fixed input format of one EEG and one EOG channel.",
    "U-Sleep's performance dropped substantially when input channels deviated from its design choice.",
    "There was an average macro F1 decrease of 0.160–0.203 when swapping the order of EEG and EOG channels in U-Sleep.",
    "Channel-attention modules reduced computational requirements needed to evaluate recordings with increasing channel numbers compared to U-Sleep.",
    "In AnySleep, components before attention modules are applied independently to each input channel.",
    "The number of component evaluations increases linearly with the channel count in AnySleep.",
    "U-Sleep handles increasing channel numbers by performing additional full model evaluations with subsequent majority voting.",
    "AnySleep's high-resolution predictions could represent short sleep events, such as arousals, which are usually missed in conventional 30-s staging.",
    "High-frequency predictions captured transitions between sleep states more accurately than 30-s epochs.",
    "Fine-grained sleep stage predictions provided micro-architectural information useful for distinguishing between age groups, sexes, and between patients with obstructive sleep apnea and healthy controls.",
    "AnySleep achieves optimal performance by adaptively combining channel information at multiple network depths.",
    "The model can shift its focus across channels and modalities at different feature abstraction levels.",
    "Gradual fusion strategies are consistent with the idea that EEG and EOG channels provide complementary information at different temporal and spatial scales.",
    "Individual channel-attention modules can assign a dominant weight to a single channel, with average weights of up to 88%.",
    "The model can reliably identify particularly informative modalities or brain regions across recordings.",
    "When averaging attention across all modules, the mean weights were similar for all four channels.",
    "AnySleep integrates information from all available EEG and EOG channels rather than relying on a single modality or channel.",
    "AnySleep's macro F1 increased with the number of available EEG channels, reaching 0.771 when six EEG and one EOG channels were provided.",
    "When the EOG channel was omitted and replaced with an additional EEG derivation, performance decreased slightly but consistently.",
    "An additional modality (EOG) provides more complementary information than adding another EEG channel.",
    "AnySleep's reliable performance across heterogeneous cohorts and montages, flexible input format, and high-frequency predictions make it a flexible foundation for large-scale, multi-center sleep studies."
] 

