    "Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD) is insufficient for evaluating Graph Generative Models (GGMs) despite its widespread use.",
    "MMD fails to capture essential structural characteristics that differentiate graph domains.",
    "The proposed Representation-aware Graph-generation Model evaluation (RGM) methodology addresses these limitations through a more comprehensive evaluation approach.",
    "MMD typically measures the similarity between distributions of selected graph properties.",
    "MMD fails to adequately assess the quality of generated graphs in preserving complex structural characteristics.",
    "Models can achieve low MMD values across various topological metrics while failing to capture the essential structural properties that define different graph classes.",
    "MMD often relies on comparing simple statistical properties like degree distribution or clustering coefficient.",
    "Simple statistical properties are insufficient to capture the complexity of real-world graphs.",
    "MMD measures similarity between feature representations in a reproducing kernel Hilbert space (RKHS).",
    "MMD reduces complex graph structure to a limited set of predetermined features.",
    "RGM leverages Geometric Deep Learning models specifically designed for graph classification tasks.",
    "RGM allows evaluation of more complex structural characteristics.",
    "RGM evaluates how well generated graphs preserve the structural characteristics that distinguish different graph domains.",
    "RGM provides a more thorough evaluation by comparing state-of-the-art Graph Generative Models on custom datasets combining synthetic and real-world graphs.",
    "The comparison includes GRAN and EDGE models.",
    "RGM reveals significant limitations in GGMs' ability to preserve essential structural properties.",
    "Traditional MMD metrics can suggest good performance even when structural properties are not preserved.",
    "This evaluation framework enables researchers to move beyond simple statistical measures.",
    "The framework better captures the complex structural properties that make graphs from different domains distinguishable.",
    "This has important implications for advancing the field of graph generation."
] 

