Statements:
[
    "Quantum canaries enable black-box auditing of quantum machine learning (QML) models through a novel approach that detects memorization and quantifies privacy leakage without requiring access to model internals.",
    "The method establishes a precise mathematical relationship between canary offset parameters and empirical privacy budget consumption.",
    "Quantum canaries are specially crafted quantum states designed to detect if a QML model has memorized specific training inputs.",
    "Offset-encoded quantum states are created using angle encoding schemes with controlled perturbations (offset parameter θ) where one encoding scheme ϕ₁ is applied to original data and a slightly different scheme ϕ₂ is applied to create neighboring states.",
    "Some quantum canaries are inserted into the training data and then reintroduced during testing to detect memorization behavior.",
    "The framework establishes a rigorous mathematical connection between the canary offset parameter and trace distance bounds, which directly relates to privacy budget consumption.",
