Statements:
[
    "GRAFT (Grid-Aware Forecasting with Text) implements sophisticated alignment mechanisms between external textual data and power load signals to enable effective multi-scale load forecasting.",
    "The system's approach to alignment and its use of position-aware cross-attention are critical for achieving superior forecasting performance.",
    "GRAFT achieves strict temporal and regional alignment through several coordinated strategies.",
    "All timestamps are unified to AEST/AEDT (Australian Eastern Standard/Daylight Time) and deduplicated in sorted order to ensure consistent temporal alignment.",
    "Text data is at daily resolution and is precisely aligned to the half-hour load data through a 'same-day broadcasting' strategy where daily text vectors are broadcast to all 48 half-hour intervals within the same day.",
    "Training samples are constructed using a sliding window approach where the calendar day at the end of the window serves as an alignment anchor, ensuring consistent temporal context.",
    "The system strictly aligns news, social media, and policy texts with half-hourly load data by 'date–region' pairs, ensuring that only relevant regional information affects the corresponding regional load forecasts.",
    "Each text source is processed with region-specific information, allowing the model to account for different regional responses to the same external events.",
    "The position-aware cross-attention mechanism is critical for multi-scale forecasting accuracy.",
    "Rather than using static concatenation or global weighting of external information, GRAFT employs cross-attention between external memory and half-hour load representations.",
    "The system implements gating and temporal-decay mechanisms that allow news and social media sources to adaptively allocate their influence at different positions, preventing the amplification of relative errors that can occur with simple linear fusion.",
    "GRAFT leverages Generalized Sparse Hopfield (GSH) networks to process multi-scale temporal patterns through the TimeGSH and SeriesGSH representations.",
    "The system implements position-dependent reading and injection of textual information, allowing different types of external information to influence different temporal scales.",
    "News affects hourly patterns more, while policies affect monthly trends.",
    "Previous methods often lacked mechanisms for acquiring, filtering, and strictly time-aligning unstructured text, leading to mismatches between when text influences load.",
    "GRAFT's approach makes it possible to answer when, where, and with what intensity text affects curve patterns and peak-valley positions, significantly improving interpretability.",
    "GRAFT consistently enhances load-forecasting accuracy across multiple time scales while maintaining robustness across different regions.",
    "This structured approach to temporal and regional alignment, coupled with position-aware cross-attention, enables GRAFT to outperform both traditional numerical models and state-of-the-art LLM-based approaches while maintaining computational efficiency suitable for practical deployment."
] 

