Statements:
[
    "AnySleep employs an innovative channel-agnostic attention mechanism that enables robust sleep staging across heterogeneous EEG and EOG configurations while supporting high temporal resolution analysis.",
    "This approach overcomes significant limitations in traditional sleep staging systems.",
    "Each input channel (whether EEG or EOG) is initially processed through separate encoder blocks to generate channel-specific feature maps at increasing levels of abstraction.",
    "Channel-attention modules then combine these channel-specific feature maps into cross-channel representations using learnable attention weights that dynamically determine each channel's relevance to the sleep staging task.",
    "This approach allows AnySleep to handle any number and choice of EEG and EOG channels, from single-channel to multi-channel recordings.",
    "When tested across different channel permutations, AnySleep showed remarkably stable performance (macro F1 scores in a narrow range of 0.726–0.760 for two-channel configurations).",
    "Even with just a single channel (e.g., one EEG derivation), AnySleep maintained high performance, with the lowest score of 0.710 for a single occipital EEG.",
    "The model's performance increases with the number of available EEG channels, reaching 0.771 macro F1 score with six EEG and one EOG channel.",
    "AnySleep's segment classifier produces sleep stage predictions at configurable frequencies up to 128 Hz, corresponding to a minimum temporal resolution of about 0.008 seconds per prediction.",
    "Unlike alternative approaches that require multiple forward passes for multi-channel data, AnySleep's attention mechanism enables a single forward pass regardless of channel count, improving computational efficiency.",
    "During training, the model randomly varies both the number and type of input channels, encouraging robustness to heterogeneous montages.",
    "For each batch, the number of channels is sampled based on a probability distribution, followed by uniform selection of available channels regardless of type (EEG or EOG).",
    "The model learns to assign different weights to different channel types across various attention modules, enabling adaptive information integration.",
    "This innovative channel-agnostic approach with high temporal resolution makes AnySleep particularly valuable for large-scale, multi-center sleep studies where recording montages may vary significantly, while still enabling the detection of fine-grained sleep events that conventional 30-second epoch scoring would miss."
] 

